        <p>littcmpt to Commit Suicide by Drinking A Ead case of a Carbolic 011. %Eard at tl young girl's attempted sliicide was ie Borough Police Court on Tuesday, before (1579110 r Roberts and other magistrates. Lily Brown 'ychiji_asugliter of Joseph Brown, gas works stoker, 4 a -(ml7r , , on-street, was charged with having drunk was of carbolic oil at 56, Amelia-street. where she stiPloyed by a Mrs. Olaham. as domestic servant. tnornierintendent Williamson said that the previous with Mrs. thR M Oldham had occasion to remonstrate low_ the girl about not performing her work " satisfac- s,'). About one p.m. the defendant was carving some Riv: end cut her finger. Shortly after the girl was look° a week's notice. Later Mrs. Oldham went to hai for the girl, who was supposed to be in the kitchen ws‘hng dinner. She was not there, and Mrs. Oldham fit). tiPstairs and found the girl on the bed. w "a was a strong smell of carbolic oil and a bottle f°n • tote ,nd in the room. The girl had also written a ress Iwhich was not read). On being asked for the the " of her action,the girl replied that it was because tnistress spoke to her. Mr. Oldham at once gave Lin girl an emetic, and she was later taken to the Forn'ar.y. e d r e,ghteen months the girl as employed at Cock- and left about Christmas. She refused to Ehe ink and on being remonstrated with by her mother, VO4.vheat out to a chemist and obtained four penny- ofven laudanum which she drank. She was then auk' ahn emetic. The mother of the girl said she was ,Nlr!"kt' 0°137 she was very sensitive when spoken to. and !°wn said her daughter was very self-willed, to heart everything that was said to her. 01.diihc:igt:arglasiani:d she took the carbolic oil because Mrs. to d ara shouted at her. She promised the Bench not r have Chairman : I am sure you could not possibly wse,,nriderstood what 3 thing you were doing or you •zt:.ci not have done it. eiN: girl was handed over to her parents, and the 14,,,',a1an told her she must realiz