        <p>REGRETTED HIS RASHNESS. Singular Case of Attempted Suicide. At (II !qr. e Warrington Police Court on Thursday, before bttni,,T J. Jolley and other magistrates, Sarah Ann t'rde —B, 24, Hobson-street, was granted a separation of With an allowance of 10s. per week on the ground .C,rsiatent cruelty of her husband, Wm. Daniels. othe;equel was beard yesterday, before the Mayor and bripi„. magistrates, when Daniels was charged with oe, attempted to commit suicide by cutting his 'rh4bS Previous afternoon. bief Constable said that P.C. Matthews was in 'iLo'ester-road about 3.30 when Mrs. Daniels asked Atte go to her husband who was creating a disturb- tsorr;inhs informed the officer about the case that v.""g, and on Matthews going to the house, prisoner kaot ',rY argumentative. He suddenly went over to the koifeet shelf and attempted to cut his throat with a hold A struggle ensued and the prisoner tried to get throjt a razor. Ile made a slight scratch across his hold n'fabd told the officer that if he could have got Qiiza, the knife he would have done something to say,, In reply to the charge, he said, "I have nothing Pr 6 thf, —eller said that when he went down the street all thiri.neighbours were out, which was a very unusual ttltie knocked at his door, but got no reply. His l said her mother was in the house, but was to tetag to let him (prisoner) in. He put his shoulder tiler: door and got in. He found his mother-in-law ths '",ho had caused all the bother. He asked to stay 15014.1.8ut, hut the mother-in-law sent his wife out for a thio—kman. He regretted his rash act, for it was a „ ,had always had a mental dread of. 4s, "JaSor : You see the folly of it ?—Prisoner : No „,e. ''aYor : You can quite see that the circutii- takiog-8,Y,0u have placed yourself in do not warrant you Pri Your life. 'ad soner • • Yes. He added that he had always been p,"113 children. 'del Constable: He told the children that he Ns " the mother in. 14 0 °ter: Dear ! Dear! You are trying to make That as a lunatic. e‘hf Constable : That ii what I am suggesting. lO : Anyone doing that must have been I.°rarily insane, I think it is very hard to try to make „:ntatic. :tts`-fl'ef Constable said it was a very serious suicide. It led one to think that there was Iliihi,ulstion but what his mind was temporarily pr'.3Rsd. '‘ltcl:°4r was sent to the Workhouse on al4 days'</p>
