        <p>last three years, and that I have never felt s' from him in spirit lf there abc)il time of favourable re-action, I should ranch I knowing that all his kindly sentiments are I now when his hour draws near, and mine c3l be far distant." The biographer, with true instinct for thl that matter, selects the following from let' telegrams that" came from all manner of Pe°l the Queen downwards" "I trust I may be permitted notwitbf temporary political differences, to express 0351'_ sympathy with you in your illness and IlaY for a speedy and secure recovery. Your grew to our people can never he forgotten, for it Ireland Inid fewest friends that your voice s sce-riti on her side. I hope you may still be 5103.r0, it on her behalf according to your concepu° is best, for while we go on struggli°g for c views, there can be nothing but regrets on st for the sharpness of division in the 13'1 obedient servant, Tilt HEALEY."</p>
