        <p>IT</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>hoe, and finest value. Nok of patent cap, crimped vamp, quarter. Fits snugly to the TDows FOR SUMMER SHOW Address: St. Paul's Street. Leeds. cc) LTD</p>
        <p>Under the Clock, Bridge Street,</p>
        <p>THINGS THAT MATTER:</p>
        <p>FEE DAYLIGHT SAVING BILL.</p>
        <p>Stockton Heath.</p>
        <p>Mr. Filson Young, in a recent contribution to the "Pall Mall Gazette," under the heading of " The Things that Matter "says : "This is the time of the year when, if you get up on a fine morning an hour or two earlier than is your usual custom you are aware of the agreeable sensation of feeling younger and lighter-hearted than usual: and, thouo the sensation does not last throughout the day, you wish sincerely that it might. That is where the almost infinite value of the measure advocated in Mr. Willett's Daylight Saving Bill lies. Most unfortunately, since it is one of the!i measures in which no political interest is involvea, and which has never been put before the public with sufficient vigour and seriousness to make it useful in attracting votes, no Government or party has any great interest. in forwarding it. Like all measures which are not politics, but merely wisdom and commonsense, there is little room for it in the political machine. The idea is still treated by a number of people as a rather attractive joke, and there are others who think in a muddled kind of way that it is merely a device for compelling them to get up earlier in the morning, before the rest of the world is up, or the machinery of life has commenced. Whereas, it simply means beginning the day in finer weather, and living in those sunlit hours of which each one of Lis has but a limited span, and not one of which, when we let it pass unlived and unenjoyed, can ever by any means be restored to us. The real value of the Day- light Saving Bill would be that if it were passed, England would immediately become a younger and happier nation. And is that not worth while ? "</p>
        <p>W. IKNlCriarr. Cycle and Motor Depot,</p>
