        <p>By Order of Executors. TO BE SOLD BY AUCTION, By Mr. A. 11. OLIVE, At the Blue Bell Inn, WARRING EON, on Wednesday next, the 4th day of June, 1913, at Five o'clock in the afternoon : LOT I.—All that well-situated DWELLING-HOUSE, No. 35, Arpley-street, Warrington. in the occupation of Mr. James Critchley as tenant thereof. Tenure leasehold for the residue of a term of 987 years from 1885, subject to the yearly ground rest of £3 18s. The above dwelling-housit beink centrally situated and in good condition offers a very desirable investment. Lo T 2.—A1l those Two DWELLING-HOUSES, situate Nos. 65 and 67,, Knutsford-road, Warrington. Gross annual rentals, £4l 123. Tenure leasehold for 999 years from 1897. Yearly ground rent, £7. The above premises are in first-class order, situated on a main road and well adapted for business purposes. For further particulars apply to the Auctioneer; or to ARTHUR J. WILLETT, 11, Lyme-street, Warrington.</p>
